<h1>Free Digital Skills to Learn</h1>
<p>Digital skills can help beginners prepare for office jobs, customer support, freelancing and other career opportunities. Start with free learning resources and regular practice.</p>

<h2>1. Email and Professional Communication</h2>
<p>Learn to write clear emails, attach files, use appropriate subject lines and communicate politely with employers.</p>

<h2>2. Documents and Word Processing</h2>
<p>Practise preparing CVs, letters, reports and formatted documents. Learn headings, page layout, tables and PDF export.</p>

<h2>3. Spreadsheets</h2>
<p>Start with rows, columns, sorting, filters, basic formulas and simple tables. These skills are useful in administration and data-related work.</p>

<h2>4. Online Research</h2>
<p>Learn to find official websites, compare information and identify trustworthy sources. Verify job vacancies directly with employers.</p>

<h2>5. Customer Support Skills</h2>
<p>Practise polite written responses, active listening, problem-solving and accurate record keeping. Improve typing speed gradually.</p>

<h2>6. Video Meetings and Teamwork</h2>
<p>Learn to join meetings, mute your microphone, share documents safely and communicate clearly with colleagues.</p>

